    [BugFix][Test] Fix renamed context-parallel flags in A5 MLA fixture (#19895)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    #19334 renamed the context-parallel flags to `use_pcp` and `use_dcp`,
    but the A5 strided MLA KV writer fixture still initialized `pcp_enabled`
    and `dcp_enabled`. Because the fixture constructs `AscendMLAImpl` with
    `__new__()`, it bypasses the constructor and fails when workspace
    preparation reads the renamed attributes.
    
    Update both fixture fields to restore the existing 18 A5 tests. The
    [main A5 nightly
    failure](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40340169158/job/121815586357)
    reported 18 setup errors with `AttributeError: 'AscendMLAImpl' object
    has no attribute 'use_pcp'`.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This changes only two field names in
    `test_mla_strided_kv_writer_a5.py`. Operator implementations,
    assertions, test parameters, and CI workflows are unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Validated on Ascend950PR (A5, x86_64), Python 3.11.10, PyTorch
    2.10.0+cpu, torch_npu 2.10.0.post7, and Triton Ascend 3.6.0:
    
    ```bash
    python -m pytest -sv -ra tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops/test_mla_strided_kv_writer_a5.py
    ```
    
    - Before the fix: reproduced the same missing-`use_pcp` setup error
    (stopped after the first error).
    - After the fix: **18 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed, 0 errors**. This
    covers 16 writer-parity cases and 2 graph-replay cases. Pytest reported
    5.03 seconds; process wall time including startup/imports was 23.11
    seconds.
    - Operator Python source hashes were unchanged during validation.
    - Ruff 0.14.0 lint/format and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci`; it could not complete because the
    connection was reset while pre-commit installed the actionlint
    environment on Windows. Full repository checks remain for CI.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Existing token counts 1, 128,
    129, and 257 and both cache layouts are retained.
    - [x] **Regression test**: The existing affected test reproduces the
    setup error before the fix and passes after it; no duplicate test was
    added.
    - [x] **Error / failure path coverage**: Reproduced the original
    missing-attribute setup failure before applying the fix.
    - [x] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: Existing writer-parity and
    graph-replay assertions are unchanged and pass on A5.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: Not applicable; this only updates
    test-fixture attribute names.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
